Changed `drain()` to copy the backing array with `slice()` and reset its length once, so it's O(n) instead of the O(n²) repeated `shift()`. FIFO order is preserved, the queue empties, and an empty queue still yields `[]` (no need for a special branch — slice on an empty array is empty). Added a test draining 20,000 items in order, plus a second drain returning empty. All 66 tests pass.
